This PR enables the usage of `@before` and `@after` method decorators using callbacks

```javascript
    import { before, after } from '@themost/events';
    class UserAction {
        constructor() {
            this.status = 'unknown';
        }
        
        @before((event, callback) => {
            void setTimeout(() => {
                event.target.status = 'loaded';
                return callback();
            }, 1000);
        })
        load(callback) {
            this.status = 'loading';
            return callback();
        }        
    }
    const item = new UserAction();
    item.load(() => {
        console.log('Loaded', 'status', item.status);
    });
```

- fixed leak caused by return from env_get();
- fixed unset and export stopping if var with wrong name;
- fixed return signal.
